{
  "about": "How a run reads the records behind a value, moved from execution_key_selection_semantics.rs and execution_filtered_mapping_source.rs at 144fc5559. The first file's tests compared each issue at its phase, condition, rule, spec paths and context, the saved out.csv, the run's handler counts as the report's handler rows name them (SPEC_PATH, NAME, COUNT), and the check rows of a failed run's saved report; the second file's compared complete issue rows and the saved bytes. A pattern read from data is checked on every row or record its predicate is asked about (FORMULA-7, CHECK-12, COLUMN-2), and the report keeps the row count check that held before it (CHECK-23). Without row templates, a column counts the distinct raw readings of a key's records (COLUMN-2); records missing a key stay apart until the output gate (OUTPUT-3); a source's order_by and keep keep one present reading, ties in record order, counting one choice per key (COLUMN-12, COLUMN-14, VALUE-22, VALUE-23). A lookup evaluates every match value before it reads a record (LOOKUP-25) and compares calendar values and numbers exactly (VALUE-19, VALUE-21). A mapping, cut or first_available source carries the filter, order_by and keep of a plain source binding, and an unpaired order_by or keep is refused (LOOKUP-10). No engine output supplied these values.",
